{"vid":"HHLfkHkUc14","source":"HHLfkHkUc14.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.1,"txt":"Hello Neil."},{"t":0.7,"txt":"Hi Georgie. How are you?"},{"t":2.1,"txt":"I'm very well, thank you. How are you?"},{"t":3.7,"txt":"I'm excellent, thank you."},{"t":4.9,"txt":"Good. Neil, have you ever had a bad or difficult job?"},{"t":9.2,"txt":"Oh yes. There's one in particular that I remember."},{"t":14,"txt":"Ooh, that's intriguing."},{"t":15.6,"txt":"I'm sure we're going to hear about it a bit later"},{"t":18.4,"txt":"because that's what we're talking about today"},{"t":20.3,"txt":"in Real Easy English – bad or difficult jobs we've had."},{"t":24.5,"txt":"Yes, and people should remember that they can get a free worksheet"},{"t":28.9,"txt":"for this podcast at bbclearningenglish.com."},{"t":32.1,"txt":"That's right."},{"t":40.2,"txt":"So Neil, tell us all about your bad or difficult job."},{"t":44.8,"txt":"Well, what happened was I found a job picking beans on a student holiday"},{"t":56.1,"txt":"while I was in Canada."},{"t":57.6,"txt":"Ooh. On a farm?"},{"t":59.5,"txt":"Yeah, but we had to travel a long way."},{"t":62.6,"txt":"And when we got there, we discovered that you got paid"},{"t":67.1,"txt":"by the amount that you picked."},{"t":69.9,"txt":"OK."},{"t":71.2,"txt":"And it cost $10 to get to this place on the coach"},{"t":74.5,"txt":"and we worked really hard all day."},{"t":76.9,"txt":"And then I got my beans and weighed them."},{"t":79.8,"txt":"And I got paid $8."},{"t":82.7,"txt":"Oh wow."},{"t":83.6,"txt":"Was it a full day's work?"},{"t":85,"txt":"Oh yeah. Hard, hard work in the heat, in a field."},{"t":89.5,"txt":"Was it fun, at least?"},{"t":90.9,"txt":"Were you with friends?"},{"t":92.2,"txt":"It's a good story now..."},{"t":94,"txt":"OK."},{"t":95.4,"txt":"...but at the time, it was very annoying."},{"t":99.8,"txt":"Exhausting, it sounds."},{"t":100.7,"txt":"It was exhausting."},{"t":101.7,"txt":"All day in the heat."},{"t":104,"txt":"I had quite a difficult job – it was just a temporary one."},{"t":108.5,"txt":"I was working in customer service, so I had to pick up calls from customers"},{"t":115.1,"txt":"who were needing help or were unhappy about the service they had."},{"t":120.5,"txt":"OK. That sounds interesting."},{"t":122.1,"txt":"What didn't you like about this job?"},{"t":125.1,"txt":"Well, the company was having a difficult time, so many or most"},{"t":130.9,"txt":"of the customers that were calling were unhappy about the service,"},{"t":136,"txt":"and so I had to talk to people who were very angry,"},{"t":140.8,"txt":"and it felt like they were angry with me, even though it wasn't my fault."},{"t":148.4,"txt":"The company changed the warehouse where they kept the products"},{"t":152.2,"txt":"and the delivery company at the same time,"},{"t":155.2,"txt":"so it was just all a big mess and I found it really stressful."},{"t":160.8,"txt":"Yeah, you say stressful."},{"t":163,"txt":"How else did it make you feel?"},{"t":165.8,"txt":"It made me feel very anxious because I took it too personally."},{"t":173,"txt":"Like I said, it felt like they were angry with me,"},{"t":175.4,"txt":"even though I had nothing to do with it."},{"t":177.9,"txt":"If you heard somebody else talking about this kind of job,"},{"t":182.3,"txt":"what advice would you give them?"},{"t":185.6,"txt":"Ooh, I would say, don't take it to heart."},{"t":189.6,"txt":"As I said, I was taking it too personally,"},{"t":193.1,"txt":"but you need to realise that you can only do your best."},{"t":197.1,"txt":"And at the end of the day, you can go home and enjoy yourself, relax,"},{"t":202.8,"txt":"and tomorrow is a new day."},{"t":205.2,"txt":"That's a very positive attitude."},{"t":207,"txt":"Yes."},{"t":207.8,"txt":"What advice would you give to people doing the job that you had in Canada?"},{"t":213.8,"txt":"I think it's really important to do some research before you say yes to a job,"},{"t":221.3,"txt":"if you're lucky to be able to choose."},{"t":224.7,"txt":"So, probably find out how much you're going to get paid, what it means,"},{"t":231.4,"txt":"and how much you have to pay to get to the place to do the job."},{"t":236.5,"txt":"Yeah, that's very important."},{"t":237.6,"txt":"And that's some good advice."},{"t":246.1,"txt":"OK. So, let's recap the vocabulary that we used in the conversation."},{"t":250.9,"txt":"Good idea."},{"t":251.9,"txt":"We had a few adjectives to describe work."},{"t":255.4,"txt":"You said that your job was stressful."},{"t":258.1,"txt":"I did. So, you can describe something as 'stressful',"},{"t":262.6,"txt":"and the emotion that you feel is 'stressed'."},{"t":266.2,"txt":"You said that your job was exhausting,"},{"t":269,"txt":"so it was very hard work, so you got very tired doing it."},{"t":273.3,"txt":"That's 'exhausting' and the feeling is 'exhausted'."},{"t":277.8,"txt":"Yeah. And I think I also said my job was annoying."},{"t":281.5,"txt":"Yes."},{"t":283.1,"txt":"And if something is annoying, it makes you feel annoyed."},{"t":288.4,"txt":"Yes, that's right. I also used the expression 'take something personally',"},{"t":292.6,"txt":"which is when you feel that someone is angry with you"},{"t":295.8,"txt":"when they're actually angry at the situation."},{"t":298.6,"txt":"Yeah. And you used another expression with a similar meaning –"},{"t":303,"txt":"'take something to heart'."},{"t":305,"txt":"If you take something to heart, just as you explained, you feel bad."},{"t":309.6,"txt":"You feel someone is attacking you, but it's just the job."},{"t":313.6,"txt":"OK. Well, that is the end of this episode of Real Easy English,"},{"t":317.4,"txt":"but Neil we'll be back next week, won't we?"},{"t":319.6,"txt":"We will. Thank you for listening and goodbye."},{"t":321.6,"txt":"Goodbye!"}],"words":[{"t":0.12,"w":"Hello"},{"t":0.12,"w":"Neil."},{"t":0.68,"w":"Hi"},{"t":0.68,"w":"Georgie."},{"t":0.68,"w":"How"},{"t":0.68,"w":"are"},{"t":0.68,"w":"you?"},{"t":2.08,"w":"I'm"},{"t":2.08,"w":